# The five projects are submodules (docs/PUBLISHING.md). They were listed here as ignored paths
# until they had commits and remotes, because until then there was nothing for a .gitmodules to
# record - and an ignored path cannot be added as a submodule, so those lines came out at the
# same moment these went in.

# No `__pycache__/` or `*.pyc` rule, deliberately. There is no Python in this repository and
# there is not meant to be - the checks and the build scripts are shell. An ignore rule for
# bytecode is a quiet accommodation for a language that is not allowed here: it would hide the
# first stray file rather than let `git status` show it.

# Claude Code's per-person overrides. `settings.json` beside it IS shared - SELFish uses it to
# deny reads and edits of `escalation.*` - but the `.local` one is whoever is sitting here, and
# tracking it means their overrides arrive in everybody else's clone. SELFish had it committed
# as a byte-identical copy of the shared file, which is the shape this prevents.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Whatever the person editing this happens to run. None of it is anybody else's business,
# and every one of these has been committed to some repository by accident at least once.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
